00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:37.770
So, there's a standard
concept in contracts that says

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:41.270
you have to have consideration
for a valid contract.

00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:44.050
Consideration is just some thing of value

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:45.950
that is exchanged between parties.

00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:48.460
Really what it's done is to prevent people

00:06:48.460 --> 00:06:50.570
from having what is called
a gratuitous contract,

00:06:50.570 --> 00:06:53.140
where you write down a contract, but,

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:55.350
it's only the one side doing something

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:57.470
and the other side isn't
getting anything as a result.

00:06:57.470 --> 00:07:00.630
So, the famous example is an uncle who

00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:05.300
tried to contract with his
nephew to go to college,

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:07.100
and the uncle isn't necessarily

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:08.890
getting anything out of that,

00:07:08.890 --> 00:07:12.540
but the law doesn't wanna have
enforceable contracts where

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:14.440
both sides don't get something out of it

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:16.660
and that thing is called consideration.

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:19.690
So, the fact that Kanye is
saying "We need consideration."

00:07:19.690 --> 00:07:21.440
and this person is saying that Kanye

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:24.647
is ready to teach 1L
contracts is so funny.

