00:08:31.810 --> 00:08:33.156
Judge: That makes sense to me.

00:08:33.156 --> 00:08:34.845
So, let's go to trial.

00:08:34.845 --> 00:08:37.320
Motion for summary judgment granted.

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:39.520
This may not make sense to everyone, but,

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:41.700
this is absolutely fantastic.

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:44.390
A summary judgment motion is
basically a trial on paper.

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:46.500
You submit your best arguments

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:49.930
and the other side submits
their best arguments, and,

00:08:49.930 --> 00:08:51.840
the thing about a summary
judgment motion is

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:56.080
that the factual basis must
be uncontested by both sides.

00:08:56.080 --> 00:08:58.290
So, if there is an issue of material fact

00:08:58.290 --> 00:09:00.200
that both sides disagree about

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:04.000
you can't grant summary judgment
and it has to go to trial.

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:06.050
That is great when you
are a defense lawyer

00:09:06.050 --> 00:09:08.890
like I tend to be, but, you know,

00:09:08.890 --> 00:09:10.360
I've been on the other
side of that as well,

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:12.520
on the plaintiff's side, and it sucks

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:16.283
when the judge grants
summary judgment against you.

